# A turn ended by Time Stop goes through its cleanup step in full (CR 724.1d, 514.1): Bot1, whose turn Bot2 ends, holds
# eight cards and discards one, which triggers Marauding Mako. A trigger waiting in the cleanup step gives players
# priority there (CR 514.3a): Bot1 casts Shore Up on the Mako while the trigger is on the stack. Once the stack is empty
# and both pass, another cleanup step begins, and it ends Shore Up's "until end of turn" effect (CR 514.2): on Bot2's
# turn 10 the Mako is a 2/2, its base 1/1 with one +1/+1 counter, not the 3/3 Shore Up made it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Marauding Mako
Mox Sapphire
Shore Up
Island x3
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Sol Ring
Time Stop
Island x10

[Actions]
